From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 02 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] python-tests: stop rebuilding via maturin develop in the imgsize fixture

The session-scoped `imgsize` fixture in python-tests/conftest.py runs
`maturin develop --manifest-path ROOT/Cargo.toml` before importing the
module. That is the right thing for a local dev loop, but under
cibuildwheel it means the test step silently recompiles the extension
from the checkout and tests *that* build, rather than the wheel
cibuildwheel just produced and installed into the isolated test venv -
defeating the point of testing the built artifact.

Drop the rebuild step and import the already-installed module instead.
The virtualenv assertion is untouched, and every other test in
python-tests/ (test_apis.py, test_sample_files.py) is unmodified and now
genuinely exercises the installed riscv64 wheel.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CI harness only: skips the maturin-develop rebuild in the test fixture so the suite exercises the already-built wheel instead of recompiling from source]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
diff --git a/python-tests/conftest.py b/python-tests/conftest.py
--- a/python-tests/conftest.py
+++ b/python-tests/conftest.py
@@ -1,7 +1,6 @@
 import sys
 from importlib import import_module
 from pathlib import Path
-from subprocess import check_call

 import pytest

@@ -11,5 +10,4 @@ ROOT = Path(__file__).parent.parent
 @pytest.fixture(scope="session")
 def imgsize():
     assert sys.prefix != sys.base_prefix, "must be in virtualenv"
-    check_call(["maturin", "develop", "--manifest-path", ROOT / "Cargo.toml"])
     return import_module("imgsize")
